# TYPEWRITER — THE FUTURE OF WRITING, REIMAGINED IN 3D

## 1. ROLE AND PRIMARY OBJECTIVE

Act as a world-class creative director, 3D interaction designer, product designer, UI/UX architect, animation specialist, and full-stack web developer.

Build a complete, highly polished, fully functional website named **TYPEWRITER**.

TYPEWRITER is an immersive, three-dimensional writing and publishing environment where people create, edit, organize, and preserve their writing as beautiful virtual physical books.

This is not a conventional journaling website. It must not look like a standard productivity dashboard with flat cards, text boxes, a sidebar, and a few buttons.

Imagine combining a luxurious antique library, a futuristic spatial-computing interface, a beautifully restored mechanical typewriter, and the versatility of a modern document editor.

The central concept is simple:

**Your ideas are written on paper. Your paper becomes pages. Your pages become books. Your books become your personal library.**

Users should be able to create as many books as their available storage plan supports, including diaries, journals, research reports, novels, manuscripts, study notes, travel logs, personal letters, professional documents, and entirely custom books.

Every book has a physical-looking three-dimensional form, a cover, a spine, pages, and its own editable content. Users can organize their creations on virtual bookshelves, open them, continue writing, edit old entries, and retrieve their work whenever they return.

The website should be visually astonishing without sacrificing practical usability.

The result must feel like an entirely new category of digital product: a living library where a real writing workflow is combined with cinematic 3D interaction.

Do not merely produce a beautiful prototype. Build the real application, connecting the 3D experience to working document creation, editing, organization, and persistence.

